  "body": "Found by auditing #181 against the project's own working notes after it merged. Two defects in what I shipped, one of them serious.\n\n## The serious one: the deadline is sized for the wrong thing\n\n5.50.0 stopped reasoning from committing the route — correct — but a held-reasoning attempt then looks **silent** to routing, so it inherits the first-token share: `FALLBACK_TOTAL_TIMEOUT ÷ chain length`. On the reporter's **eleven-model** sonnet route that is **54 seconds**, which is not enough time for a model to think.\n\nMeasured against the same 161,812-row log:\n\n```\nsuccessful requests that produced reasoning        105,078\n  slower than a 54.5s answer-deadline, with\n  little or no answer  -> would be diverted           1,387\n  same, against a 300s answer-deadline                   27\nbudget exhaustions that were reasoning-only              44\n```\n\n**~1,387 diversions to rescue ~44 failures** — and the tightness buys nothing, because every one of the 499 budget exhaustions ran the **full** 600s, so any allowance below that rescues all of them. On a chain of similarly slow models those diversions can cascade into outright failures.\n\n### The fix\n\n`FALLBACK_REASONING_ANSWER_TIMEOUT`, default **300s**, a flat allowance instead of a share.\n\nThe provider emits an empty heartbeat while its holdback buffer is withholding thought frames. Routing consumes it, keeps the attempt uncommitted, and starts the allowance from the **first** held thought — deliberately not re-armed per thought, because a model looping forever produces reasoning indefinitely and a stall-style clock would never fire on the exact failure this bounds.\n\nA stream that produces **nothing at all** sends no heartbeat and keeps the tight share, so the fix that took hangs from 150/day to roughly one is untouched. There is a test pinning that.\n\nThe sentinel lives in `core/anthropic/stream_contracts.py`, not the provider package — `application` may not import `providers`, and `test_import_boundaries.py` said so. Moved, not shimmed.\n\n## The other one: a number I published was wrong\n\n5.50.0 claimed \"**479 of 499** budget exhaustions\" were this mechanism. 479 is how many ran on one **model** — I grouped by `resolved_model` and read the top row as a mechanism count. Grouped by mechanism:\n\n```\nnothing at all   401   (the older scaffolding shape)\nsome answer       54\nreasoning only    44\n```\n\nOverstated ~11x. The mechanism and the reported failure are unchanged. Corrected here, in the v5.50.0 release notes, and on #181.\n\n## Also\n\n`FALLBACK_ON_REASONING_ONLY` and the new setting are now in the README beside their siblings — along with `FALLBACK_STALL_TIMEOUT`, which had never been documented since it shipped.\n\n## Verification\n\n- 8 new tests.\n- **14 mutations, 10 caught** — four of them by *hanging*, which for a deadline is the strongest possible result.\n- Three more were first reported `SKIPPED (marker count 0)` because `ruff format` had reflowed the lines my markers matched (§165). Re-run against the formatted text: all three caught.\n- One was a **broken probe** — it wrote a raw newline into a string literal and only proved the file would not parse. The property it aimed at is unkillable by construction (routing compares against the same constant), so it is asserted directly instead.\n- The first mutation run also hit the 10-minute tool cap mid-case and **left a mutation in my source**; my integrity check verified four markers and missed it. Caught by reading the formatted source, restored, and the harness now asserts the restore succeeded.\n- Full suite **5021 passed**; the 8 `test_installers.py` failures reproduce identically on unmodified `fork/main`.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- At the 300s default, ~27 slow reasoning requests in 105,078 would still divert to a fallback rather than complete on the primary. `0` disables the allowance entirely and lets a thinking model run to the whole request budget.\n- The heartbeat is a new provider→routing signal. It is empty, is not valid SSE, and is consumed before any client-facing branch; a test asserts it never reaches the client.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti",
